      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nDisable native padded decode in DeepseekV32IndexerMetadataBuilder when positive per-request decode lengths in a speculative decoding step are non-uniform, falling back to per-token flattened decode.\n\nFixes #64855\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes wrong indexer logits and top-k block selection on ragged multi-token decode batches when native padded decode is enabled without varlen or flattening.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/attention/test_indexer_native_next_n.py -v\n```\n\n## Details\n\nWhen max_decode_len > 1 and a batch mixes requests with different positive decode lengths (such as a 1-token request alongside a (1 + k)-token request after rejected draft tokens or a freshly prefilled request), the native padded path expands every request's context lengths using max_decode_len and packs queries into (B, max_decode_len) while top_k_per_row_decode reads the first batch_size * next_n rows as a dense prefix. Requiring uniform positive decode_lens for use_native routes ragged steps through the existing per-token flattening path.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's /pr-checklist skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
